GAL16V8
SSCFIXC

CLK  E    Q    NC   NC   NC   NC   NC   NC   GND
/OE  QX   C2   C1   C0   Q2   Q1   E2   E1   VCC

; SSC clock fixer rev C -- ATF16V8B, registered mode, CLK = 28.63636 MHz.
; Replaces Q on the cartridge (pin 7) with QX so the SSC's IC3 (E xor Q)
; always produces 1.79 MHz for the PIC 7040 and AY-3-8913.
;
; E1/E2, Q1/Q2  two-stage synchronizers for the CoCo E and Q.
; C2..C0        Gray-code counter of E-low/Q-low time, saturating at state 6 (101):
;                 0 000, 1 001, 2 011, 3 010, 4 110, 5 111, 6 101
;               counts while E2=0,Q2=0; clears while E2=1,Q2=0; holds while Q2=1.
;               Q rises 140 ns (fast) or 279 ns (slow) after E falls. At 34.9 ns/tick
;               the count reaches 4..5 (fast) or 6 (slow) before Q2 freezes it.
; QX            combinational: raw Q gated by "count = 6". Each count step changes
;               one bit, so the decode cannot glitch. QX follows Q within one GAL
;               delay in slow cycles and stays 0 in fast cycles.

E1.R = E
E2.R = E1
Q1.R = Q
Q2.R = Q1

C2.R = Q2 * C2
     + /E2 * /Q2 * C2
     + /E2 * /Q2 * C1 * /C0

C1.R = Q2 * C1
     + /E2 * /Q2 * /C2 * C0
     + /E2 * /Q2 * /C2 * C1
     + /E2 * /Q2 * C2 * C1 * /C0

C0.R = Q2 * C0
     + /E2 * /Q2 * /C1
     + /E2 * /Q2 * C2

QX = Q * C2 * /C1 * C0

DESCRIPTION

Speech/Sound Cartridge clock fixer, rev C. Pin 1 = 28.63636 MHz oscillator,
pin 2 = CoCo E, pin 3 = CoCo Q, pin 11 = GND, pin 12 = QX to SSC pin 7.
